On Aug 19, 2009, at 20:15, Joshua Choi wrote:

> The selma'o seem to have non-Lojbanic names like "BAhE". How does  
> one refer to a selma'o in Lojban, short of quoting?


le selma'o be zo ba'e

.i le selma'o be zo ba'e du le selma'o be zo za'e

Note that "selma'o" is the se-conversion of "cmavo"; you can use any  
cmavo in the x2 of "selma'o" to refer to its selma'o.

